tool_arguments.summary:
The floatformat filter in Django drops precision when used with Decimal numbers due to incorrect conversion to float. The issue is located in the floatformat function where Decimal values are converted to float instead of being handled as Decimals. The root cause is in the following lines of code in django/template/defaultfilters.py:

```python
try:
    input_val = repr(text)
    d = Decimal(input_val)
except InvalidOperation:
    try:
        d = Decimal(str(float(text)))
    except (ValueError, InvalidOperation, TypeError):
        return ""
```

This conversion to float can introduce precision loss, especially for numbers with many decimal places. The expected behavior is for the floatformat filter to handle Decimal values without converting them to float, preserving the original precision. A pull request has been prepared and can be found at: https://github.com/django/django/pull/15863

